- The game logic should handle user input (mouse clicks) and update the game state accordingly.
- The player controller should manage the player's actions based on the game logic.

## Code Snippet

```java
// Game Logic
public class GameLogic {
    private int mouseX;
    private int mouseY;

    public void updateMousePosition(int mx, int my) {
        mouseX = mx;
        mouseY = my;

        // Update game state based on mouse position
    }

    public boolean checkClickDown() {
        return mouseX > 0 && mouseY > 0; // Example condition
    }

    public boolean checkClickUp() {
        return mouseX == 0 || mouseY == 0; // Example condition
    }
}

// Player Controller
public class PlayerController {
    private GameLogic gameLogic;

    public PlayerController(GameLogic gameLogic) {
        this.gameLogic = gameLogic;
    }

    public void processInput() {
        if (checkClickDown()) {
            System.out.println("Left click down");
        }
        if (checkClickUp()) {
            System.out.println("Left click up");
        }
    }
}
```

